cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GridForge or the networks it builds, please cite the paper below."
title: "GridForge"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-30"
license: MIT
abstract: "GridForge builds synthetic, KCL-compliant electric transmission networks from public data. FLO-Grid builds the topology with a Garver-style network-flow linear program over every length-feasible substation pair, and SCALE-Grid sizes conductors, voltage levels and transformers with sequential DC power flow."
keywords:
  - synthetic power grids
  - transmission network construction
  - network-flow linear programming
  - power system test cases
repository-code: "https://github.com/Snodgrass-Research-Group/GridForge-Public"
authors:
